{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792406942,"nonce":"JnN7siieFwtbgoaOIcI7mIyqIqU=","title":"Preprocessor ignores define values: `-D name=value` and comparisons like `#if (haxe_ver \u003e= 4.3)`","message":"`PreprocessorConfig.defines` is a set of names. The hxml parser keeps `-D name=value` (and haxelib adds `-D lib=version`), but only the name reaches `#if`, so a condition that compares a define's value cannot be decided correctly. Haxe also defines `haxe_ver`, `haxe` and per-library version values that real code tests. Needed: defines with optional values, and comparison operators in `evaluate_condition`.","files":null}]}